```js
groupByLength(['tea', 'go', 'sun', 'be']);
// { 3: ['tea', 'sun'], 2: ['go', 'be'] }
```

interviewQuestions.modelAnswerMd:
`reduce(callback, initialValue)` walks the array and carries an **accumulator** from one step to the next. The callback receives `(accumulator, item)` and returns the new accumulator.

```js
const sum = nums.reduce((acc, n) => acc + n, 0);
const counts = words.reduce((acc, w) => {
  acc[w] = (acc[w] || 0) + 1;
  return acc;
}, {});
```

Always pass an initial value. Without it, an empty array throws an error.
